            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for wanders, then the Sanskrit for grows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: भविष्यत्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भविष्यत् — bhaviṣyat — \"the future\". Sanskrit puts the future inside the verb, with -ष्य- before the ending: पठति — \"reads\" — becomes पठिष्यति — \"will read\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bhaviṣyat is the future participle of the root √bhū \"be, become\": \"about to be\", and as a noun \"the future\" (MW). MW sets √bhū beside Latin fuit \"was\" and English be: an inherited Indo-European root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
